## 5. Analytical Workflow

### Step 1: Data Collection & Standardization

Prepare and standardize supplier, purchase order and logistics information.

Key fields include:

- Supplier ID and Supplier Name
- Purchase Order Number
- Material / Product ID
- PO Creation Date
- Promised Delivery Date
- Actual Receipt Date
- Ordered Quantity
- Received Quantity
- Contractual Lead Time
- Actual Lead Time
- Unit Purchase Price
- Reference Purchase Price
- Transportation Lane / Carrier

### Step 2: Supplier Lead-Time Analysis

Evaluate supplier delivery consistency using planned and actual lead times.

Analysis includes:

- Average supplier lead time.
- Median lead time.
- Lead-time standard deviation.
- Lead-time coefficient of variation.
- Delayed purchase order frequency.
- Supplier delivery consistency.

### Step 3: OTIF Performance Measurement

Measure whether suppliers deliver the correct quantity within the agreed delivery window.

**OTIF Formula:**

OTIF (%) = (On-Time and In-Full Deliveries / Total Eligible Deliveries) × 100

A delivery qualifies as OTIF only when it satisfies both the agreed delivery-date tolerance and the required quantity criteria.

### Step 4: Purchase Order & Freight Risk Analysis

Identify operational bottlenecks through:

- Overdue purchase order monitoring.
- Supplier delivery delays.
- Freight transportation delays.
- Carrier performance evaluation.
- Material availability risks.
- Open purchase order exposure.

### Step 5: Supplier Risk Identification

Develop transparent supplier risk indicators based on:

- Delivery reliability.
- Lead-time variability.
- OTIF performance.
- Purchase order fulfillment.
- Pricing variance.
- Freight delay frequency.

Use documented thresholds and clearly defined scoring rules to classify suppliers into risk categories.

### Step 6: Tableau Dashboard Development

Develop an interactive dashboard concept to provide procurement and supply chain management with visibility into supplier performance and logistics risks.

## 6. Key Performance Indicators (KPIs)

| KPI | Measurement |
|---|---|
| OTIF % | On-time and in-full deliveries / eligible deliveries |
| Average Lead Time | Average actual supplier lead time |
| Median Lead Time | Middle value of actual lead times |
| Lead-Time Variability | Standard deviation of supplier lead time |
| Lead-Time CV | Standard deviation / mean lead time |
| Late PO Count | Number of overdue or late purchase orders |
| Overdue PO Value | Financial value of overdue open purchase orders |
| Price Variance | Actual unit price versus approved reference price |
| Supplier Reliability | Composite supplier performance assessment |

